  "final_message": "Implemented all three versions using the specified time-step order: compute every spring force from the old state, then update velocities and positions.\n\n- [Rust](C:/Users/sandh/nb-work/39-rust-vs-python/sessions/terra/springs/rust/src/main.rs) uses contiguous vectors and compiled loops.\n- [plain.py](C:/Users/sandh/nb-work/39-rust-vs-python/sessions/terra/springs/plain.py) uses lists and direct loops with a reusable force buffer.\n- [fast.py](C:/Users/sandh/nb-work/39-rust-vs-python/sessions/terra/springs/fast.py) uses NumPy arrays and reusable buffers for vectorized operations.\n\nThe offline Rust release build succeeded. **All three versions passed all five samples:** `s1a`, `s1b`, `s1c`, `s2`, and `s3`.",
